# ── The catalogue, read off the registry rather than assumed ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ EVERY ROW IS A DIGEST, AND THE TAG IT WAS READ FROM IS RECORDED HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE. The
# containerdisks project rebuilds a tag whenever the distribution publishes a new cloud image, so a
# tag names different bytes from one week to the next; the platform offers the bytes somebody read.
# Resolved through the OCI distribution API (the same token dance charts/bundle/oci.sh does) on the
# date below, asking for the index media types first so a multi-architecture tag answers with its
# INDEX digest — the one `docker://…@sha256:` addresses. All four tags answered on the first request.
#
#   ubuntu-24.04   quay.io/containerdisks/ubuntu:24.04   sha256:1b49166bd3047c7d818be67cec73f891b12db7e792dbc91809412b6be1c20ec2
#   ubuntu-22.04   quay.io/containerdisks/ubuntu:22.04   sha256:27d3bbe1374521aa43fc50b647d712c9c90693f1e8ce9516aa25aeb73f17681d
#   debian-13      quay.io/containerdisks/debian:13      sha256:518a687c58255e8556906a6f51f45ed9e96b0997eedd6e8a12c36680d82e2956
#   debian-12      quay.io/containerdisks/debian:12      sha256:ba8d5e83785ce239fa1ff9767ee0146019b96421f96543b68b154cf9e1ff4c7f
#
catalogue-reviewed: 2026-09-17
#
# ⚠ A REGISTRY READ IS NOT A BOOTED GUEST. This establishes that each digest exists and is what the
# tag pointed at that day. It says nothing about whether the image boots on this platform — no guest
# has run here, charts/managed/virtual-machine/conformance.yaml § owed, `running-is-the-vm-lanes`.
#
# ⚠ WHY NOT THE DISTRIBUTIONS' OWN URLS. cloud-images.ubuntu.com and cloud.debian.org publish the same
# images with SHA256SUMS beside them, and CDI's HTTP importer takes no checksum — it has a URL, a
# secret and a certificate bundle. A digest in a registry reference is verified by the puller; a
# SHA256SUMS line would be a record this platform wrote down and nothing compared. The catalogue is
# therefore registry references, and the `url` source keeps HTTP for tenants who accept the
# difference (conformance.yaml § owed, `http-imports-are-unverified`).
#
# ⚠ WHY NOT ROCKY OR WINDOWS. containerdisks publishes no Rocky Linux disk; docs/plan/13 § Images and
# licensing rules Windows Server out until a licensing arrangement exists.
#
# ── What the review established about CDI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ AN IMAGE HAS NO CONSUMER, SO ON A WaitForFirstConsumer CLASS IT NEEDS
# `cdi.kubevirt.io/storage.bind.immediate.requested: "true"` OR IT NEVER IMPORTS. The annotation makes
# CDI's controller bind the claim itself; charts/managed/disk deliberately omits it.
#
# ⚠ THE DataVolume SPEC IS IMMUTABLE, as charts/managed/disk/SOURCE records, which is why every
# tenant-facing value here is @immutable.
# ⚠ AND THE ACCESS MODE HAS TO BE WRITTEN, because CDI has no StorageProfile entry for openebs.io/local
# — charts/managed/disk/SOURCE has the reading and its conformance.yaml § owed,
# `access-mode-is-read-write-once`, the cost.
upstream-webhook: CDI ships a validating webhook for DataVolume (spec immutability, exactly one source, a registry url must start with docker://) and a mutating one that fills spec.storage from the StorageProfile
